warm-start arm: A=16 hopeless @t=180, B=12 escalation @t=5, C=72 already-solved @t=5; modes ('warm', 'prior_warm')
  72 cells to run, 16 workers
    20/72  6.3 min  eta 16.3 min
    40/72  10.2 min  eta 8.2 min
    60/72  14.1 min  eta 2.8 min
    72/72  16.8 min  eta 0.0 min

=== A. capability: 16 targets no tier solves, t=180 ===
  cold baseline: 0/16; hard-pin retrieval got 1 (target 97)
  warm           2/16  solved   median start_bp  121   median moved   87   -> [60, 97]
  prior_warm     0/16  solved   median start_bp  132   median moved   88   

=== B. efficiency: 12 escalation targets at t=5 ===
  cold at t=5: 0/12 by construction; hard-pin retrieval got 4, prior 2
  warm           3/12  solved   median start_bp   31   median moved   28   -> [52, 61, 77]
  prior_warm     2/12  solved   median start_bp   31   median moved   35   -> [66, 77]

=== C. breakage: 72 targets the plain t=5 tier already solves ===
  cold: 72/72 by construction; hard-pin retrieval BROKE 25, prior BROKE 30
  warm          66/72  solved   median start_bp   28   median moved   39   
  prior_warm    65/72  solved   median start_bp   28   median moved   36   

=== D. breakage at the LAST rung: 2 targets cold t=180 solves ===
  cold t=180: 2/2 by construction -> [78, 92]
  warm           1/2   solved   median start_bp  141   median moved   82   -> [92]
  prior_warm     0/2   solved   median start_bp  141   median moved   82   

=== the shippable design: warm-start ONLY the last rung ===
  a target reaching t=180 has already failed every cheaper rung, so the cheap-tier
  breakage measured in C cannot occur; the only risk is D.
  warm         A gains 2, D breaks 1  ->  net +1 solves at ZERO extra cost (the rung is paid anyway)
  prior_warm   A gains 0, D breaks 2  ->  net -2 solves at ZERO extra cost (the rung is paid anyway)

=== SEED REPLICATION: is the +1 stable, or was it three lucky events? ===
  decision rule declared BEFORE the run: ship iff A >= 2 on EVERY seed and D breaks <= 1 on every seed.
  mode          seed  A solved/16  D broken/2   net
  warm             0            2           1    +1
  warm             1            1           1    +0
  warm             2            0           1    -1
  warm         -> DO NOT SHIP   gains [2, 1, 0], breaks [1, 1, 1], nets [1, 0, -1]
  prior_warm       0            0           2    -2
  prior_warm       1            1           1    +0
  prior_warm       2            0           1    -1
  prior_warm   -> DO NOT SHIP   gains [0, 1, 0], breaks [2, 1, 1], nets [-2, 0, -1]

